<title>CANADA: Falconbridge Falcondo workers ratify pact.</title>
<headline>Falconbridge Falcondo workers ratify pact.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian miner Falconbridge Ltd said on Wednesday that 1,100 unionized workers at its Falcondo operation in the Dominion Republic ratified a three-year contract.</p>
<p>&quot;It's been voted on and ratified and it runs until November 30, 1999,&quot; Falconbridge spokeswoman Caroline Casselman said in a phone interview.</p>
<p>The previous contract expired on November 30, 1996.</p>
<p>Falcondo is 85 percent-owned by Falconbridge, 10 percent by the government of the Dominican Republic, 4.1 percent by Redstone Resources Inc  and the rest by various individuals.</p>
<p>Falcondo's total mine production for the year ended December 31, 1996 was 3.1 million tonnes of ore.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
</text>
